From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:15:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): ask for a project when starting a new session
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A project carries the settings a new session needs (host, workspace,
agent, model, worktree), but every "new session" entry point opens a
plain composer, so filing a session in its project and getting those
defaults is an extra, easily forgotten step.

When projects exist, the new-session hotkey, the sidebar's New session
links (also reached from the mobile drawer), and the palette's New chat
now open the palette on a project step: No project first, then every
project, filtered by name as you type. Picking one opens /?project=<name>,
the route the per-project pencil already uses. Modified clicks on the
links still open the composer in a new tab, and Settings › General ›
Sessions has a switch to turn the prompt off.

The project step is offered while the project list is still loading and
closes for the plain composer when the list fails or comes back empty; a
stale session fetch error stays hidden on it. E2E tests that click New
session and expect the composer turn the prompt off
(omnigent:new-chat-project-prompt=off), and a dedicated E2E drives the
picker's No project and project rows.

Phones (below the md breakpoint) ask in a bottom sheet instead of the
palette, whose search field would raise the keyboard for a choice among a
handful of projects: a grab handle, "Start a new session in", then No
project and every project as 48px rows, with no search field. Picking a
row opens the same /?project=<name> or plain composer; tapping outside,
Escape or dragging the handle down closes it where the user was. It
follows the same switch and step-aside rule as the palette. The sheet is
a small controlled BottomSheet primitive on the Radix dialog (the UI kit
had none). Matches https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11397.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8aacafc9a2edf35cadd88651666eca630700b489)
